// "case on y" inside a case, before its sub-cases; plain cases elsewhere stay plain
let x, y in Z. wts x^2 + y^2 is not 3 mod 4
case on x
case x is even
x^2 ≡ 0 mod 4.
case on y
subcase y is even
then x^2 + y^2 ≡ 0 mod 4.
subcase y is odd
then x^2 + y^2 ≡ 1 mod 4.
case x is odd
x^2 ≡ 1 mod 4, and y^2 is 0 or 1 mod 4, so x^2 + y^2 is 1 or 2 mod 4.
in either case, x^2 + y^2 is not 3 mod 4.
qed
